    "created_at": "2020-09-11T21:25:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-09-11T21:25:03Z",
    "body": "I like the extended attribute idea. There's also precedent in [protocol buffers](https://developers.google.com/protocol-buffers/docs/proto3#options) for something like this.\r\n\r\nI would also personally prefer [Historical]. It's fine for code generators to translate [Historical] to \"deprecated\" if the generated code is user-facing (e.g., TypeScript definitions).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
